{
  "id": "contexts/self_containment/01_host_declarations",
  "topic": "contexts",
  "subtopic": "self_containment",
  "title": "Headers that need their includer",
  "summary": "A header that uses what its includer declares first still compiles, in the includer's context",
  "prose": "`ruler.h` uses a type and a macro that `main.cpp` declares before including it, so the header does not compile on its own. clice finds that out and compiles it after what `main.cpp` declares, so it has no errors and hover works inside it.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
